        "notes": "A malt-forward successor to Gulp, brewed for Daniel on 2026-08-23 and still inspired by Omaka Klunk. Brew-day measurements were 20.55 kg of wort at 1.042 SG, equivalent to 19.7 l, with 638 g Aromatic Malt used. Expect approximately 1.012 FG and 4.0% ABV if Safale S-33 reaches 72% apparent attenuation; bitterness is estimated at 36 IBU and colour at 23 EBC. Safale S-33 and the aromatic and caramel-malt charge preserve the full, gently sweet character Daniel liked, while firmer bitterness keeps it drinkable. Aromatic and Carabohemian together are 16.8% of the grist (20.5% non-base malt when the torrefied wheat is included). Target substitutes for Klunk's First Gold, while Saaz, Bramling Cross and a restrained orange-peel addition preserve the original beer's spicy, citrus and dark-fruit identity. Hop weights use the on-hand lots: Target 2020 at 9.2% alpha acid, Saaz 2022 at 2.7%, and Bramling Cross 2020 at 6.5%. Inspiration: https://www.bjcp.org/style/2021/11/11B/best-bitter/, https://www.britishhops.org.uk/varieties/target/ and https://www.britishhops.org.uk/varieties/bramling-cross/\n\nFerment at 18°C and allow a gentle rise to 19°C, keeping S-33's fruitiness restrained. Package only after gravity is stable. Carbonate gently to approximately 1.8 volumes of CO₂ and serve at 10-12°C.",
